# LAMAGUE Computational Kernel v0.5
program ControlledRelease
version 0.5
identity controlled_release_protocol
purpose "Test a bounded release without crossing an irreversible-harm boundary."
claim "A controlled pilot may proceed only while the irreversible path remains closed."
risk high
confidence 0.92
irreversible false
path K -> O -> E -> U -> I -> G -> V -> H -> S -> F -> Z -> Y

evidence safety_test "Pre-release safety test record."
evidence monitoring_plan "Active monitoring and incident capture plan."
evidence rollback_test "Verified rollback rehearsal."

unknown rare_failure protected required_for=ordinary_release
unknown long_term_effect protected required_for=ordinary_release

invariant harm_boundary "Credible irreversible harm triggers immediate provisional halt."
invariant dissent_lineage "Every position remains attributable."
invariant restart_asymmetry "No single gate may restart the system."

authority operator scope=pilot "Human operator may authorise only the bounded pilot."

participant advocate
participant safety_model
participant domain_expert
participant operator
participant silent_witness

affected pilot_participant
affected indirect_decision_subject

boundary cohort "Small monitored cohort."
boundary autonomy "No autonomous external control."
boundary rollback "Immediate rollback capability."

dissent advocate "Release now because people may benefit."
dissent safety_model "Do not release while irreversible unknowns remain."
dissent domain_expert "Proceed only through a controlled pilot."

valueflow pilot_participant research_program consent=revocable "Experience and outcome data."

recovery rollback "Restore the previous operational state."
recovery containment "Remove access and preserve incident evidence."

effect MayAffect<pilot_participant>
effect CreatesReversibleRisk
effect CallsExternalSystem<decision_support_tool>

gate affected_party
gate expert
gate operator
gate silent_witness

horizon 30_days
limit max_steps=64
compress requested
yield "Bounded monitored pilot with visible unknowns, dissent, authority, affected parties, and rollback."
